[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Modules","page":"API","text":"Order = [:module]","title":"Modules"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Types-and-constants","page":"API","text":"Order = [:type, :constant]","title":"Types and constants"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Functions-and-macros","page":"API","text":"Order = [:macro, :function]","title":"Functions and macros"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Documentation","page":"API","text":"","title":"Documentation"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EmpiricalDistributions.MvBinnedDist","page":"API","text":"MvBinnedDist <: StatsBase.Distribution{Multivariate,Continuous}\n\nA binned multivariate distribution, usually derived from a histogram.\n\nConstructors:\n\n    MvBinnedDist(h::StatsBase.Histogram{<:Real,N})\n    MvBinnedDist{T<:Real}(h::StatsBase.Histogram{<:Real,N})\n\nYou can convert a MvBinnedDist back to a histogram via \n\nconvert(StatsBase.Histogram, dist::MvBinnedDist)\nStatsBase.Histogram(dist::MvBinnedDist)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EmpiricalDistributions.MvBinnedDist"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#EmpiricalDistributions.UvBinnedDist","page":"API","text":"UvBinnedDist{T<:Real} <: StatsBase.Distribution{Univariate,Continuous}\n\nA binned univariate distribution, usually derived from a histogram.\n\nConstructors:\n\n    UvBinnedDist(h::StatsBase.Histogram{<:Real,1})\n    UvBinnedDist{T<:Real}(h::StatsBase.Histogram{<:Real,1})\n\nYou can convert a UvBinnedDist back to a histogram via \n\nconvert(StatsBase.Histogram, dist::UvBinnedDist)\nStatsBase.Histogram(dist::UvBinnedDist)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"EmpiricalDistributions.UvBinnedDist"},{"category":"section","location":"LICENSE/#LICENSE","page":"LICENSE","text":"using Markdown\nMarkdown.parse_file(joinpath(@__DIR__, \"..\", \"..\", \"LICENSE.md\"))","title":"LICENSE"},{"category":"section","location":"#EmpiricalDistributions.jl","page":"Home","text":"A Julia package for empirical probability distributions that implement the Distributions.jl API.\n\nThis package currently provides uni- and multivariate binned distributions that can be created from StatsBase.jl histograms.\n\nUvBinnedDist, usually derived from a 1-dimensional histogram, represents a binned univariate continuous distribution:\n\nusing Distributions, StatsBase\n\nX_uv = rand(Normal(2.0, 0.5), 10^5)\nuvhist = fit(Histogram, X_uv)\n\nusing EmpiricalDistributions\n\nuvdist = UvBinnedDist(uvhist)\nuvdist isa Distribution{Univariate,Continuous}\n\nThe resulting distribution can be queried, used to generate random numbers, etc.:\n\nmean(uvdist), var(uvdist)\nmaximum(uvdist), minimum(uvdist)\nrand(uvdist, 5)\n\nA binned distribution can be converted back to a histogram:\n\nusing LinearAlgebra\nHistogram(uvdist) == normalize(uvhist)\n\nMvBinnedDist, usually derived from a multidimensional histogram, represents a binned multivariate continuous distribution:\n\nX_mv = rand(MvNormal([3.5, 0.5], [2.0 0.5; 0.5 1.0]), 10^5)\nmvhist = fit(Histogram, (X_mv[1, :], X_mv[2, :]))\n\nmvdist = MvBinnedDist(mvhist)\nmvdist isa Distribution{Multivariate,Continuous}\n\nmean(mvdist), cov(mvdist)\nrand(mvdist, 5)","title":"EmpiricalDistributions.jl"}]
